IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain

-- g8-nouns: the nouns of group G8 (Articles 26 to 36 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014), and nothing else: no rule and no #EVAL lives here.
-- It holds (1) the eighteen fork enumerations and the one record that carries them, `Interpretation of Articles 26 to 36`,
-- (2) the acts of the regulative rules of Part 7 and Part 8, and (3) the group-local records that the rules of the four rule modules take as inputs.
-- Every constructor name carries the Article it belongs to, so that it cannot collide with a name from another group when the integrator composes them.
-- Field names are noun phrases, never "is ..." or "has ...": the genitive supplies the verb.

§ `Part 7 and Part 8 -- the forks of group G8`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The fork points.  One fork point is one enumeration, one constructor per reading; the first constructor of each is the reading taken.
-- Each is registered in FRAGMENT-G8.md with the text that licenses each reading and the case that tells them apart.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- F8.1: Article 26(5)(a) "a period of one year" says nothing about when the year starts.
DECLARE `When the retention year of Article 26(5) starts` IS ONE OF
    `the year of Article 26(5) runs from the day the document is provided or retained`
    `the year of Article 26(5) runs from the day of the notice`

-- F8.2: Article 26(6) "as soon as practicable" is a standard of promptness with no number.  The first reading takes it as a judgement; the other two give it a number of days from the request,
-- and differ on whether the day of the request is the first of those days.
DECLARE `How promptness under Article 26(6) is judged` IS ONE OF
    `promptness under Article 26(6) is a judgement the caller supplies`
    `promptness under Article 26(6) is a number of days from the request`
    `promptness under Article 26(6) is a number of days counting the day of the request as the first`

-- F8.3: Article 28(1)(a) "by virtue of Article 6(1)(c)"; Article 6(2)(f) makes a philosophical-belief purpose only analogous to (c).
DECLARE `Whether Article 28(1)(a) reaches a philosophical belief purpose` IS ONE OF
    `only a purpose within Article 6(1)(c) counts under Article 28(1)(a)`
    `a philosophical belief purpose also counts under Article 28(1)(a)`

-- F8.4: Article 33 lists the decisions that may be appealed.
DECLARE `Whether the list of appealable decisions in Article 33 is closed` IS ONE OF
    `the list of appealable decisions in Article 33 is closed`
    `a decision unlisted in Article 33 is appealable by analogy with a listed one`

-- F8.5: Article 35(1) gives one ground for an appeal to the court; Article 34(1) gives a wider one for the tribunal.
DECLARE `On what ground a decision of the tribunal is appealed to the court` IS ONE OF
    `a decision of the tribunal is appealed to the court only on the ground in Article 35(1)`
    `a decision of the tribunal is appealed to the court on any ground in Article 34(1)`

-- F8.6: Article 36(2)(a) lets an Order prescribe time limits and 36(2)(b) lets it provide for notice of decisions; neither says what the limit runs from.
DECLARE `From when an appeal time limit under Article 36(2) runs` IS ONE OF
    `an appeal time limit under Article 36(2) runs from the notice of the decision`
    `an appeal time limit under Article 36(2) runs from the decision`

-- F8.7: Articles 26(1) and 27(2) let the Commissioner specify a time; when the notice fixes a period of days, the Law does not say how it is counted.
DECLARE `How a period fixed by a notice under Article 26 or 27 is counted` IS ONE OF
    `the day of service is not counted in a period fixed by a notice`
    `the day of service is the first day of a period fixed by a notice`

-- F8.9: Article 26(5)(a) "a period of one year" from a start day: does the year end on the anniversary, or on the day before it?
DECLARE `Where the retention year of Article 26(5) ends` IS ONE OF
    `the year of Article 26(5) ends on the anniversary of the day it starts`
    `the year of Article 26(5) ends on the day before the anniversary of the day it starts`

-- F8.10: a year added to 29 February.
DECLARE `How a year is added to 29 February under Article 26(5)` IS ONE OF
    `a year of Article 26(5) from 29 February ends on 28 February`
    `a year of Article 26(5) from 29 February ends on 1 March`

-- F8.11: Article 29(1) "without the consent of the person to whom it relates and (where sub-paragraph (b) applies) the person from whom it was received".
DECLARE `Which consents Article 29(1) requires` IS ONE OF
    `Article 29(1) requires both consents`
    `Article 29(1) is met by either consent`

-- F8.12: the counting of an appeal time limit, once the Order (or Article 36(2)) has fixed the day it runs from and the number of days.
DECLARE `Whether the first day counts in an appeal time limit under Article 36(2)` IS ONE OF
    `the day of the anchor is not counted in an appeal time limit`
    `the day of the anchor is the first day of an appeal time limit`

-- F8.13: Article 33(5) "A person, other than an applicant for registration, a registered charity, or the Attorney General".
DECLARE `Who is excluded from appealing under Article 33(5)` IS ONE OF
    `any applicant for registration or registered charity is excluded from appealing under Article 33(5)`
    `only the applicant concerned and the charity it became are excluded from appealing under Article 33(5)`

-- F8.14: Article 27(1) "if the Commissioner believes that".
DECLARE `What Article 27(1) requires of the Commissioner's belief` IS ONE OF
    `the Commissioner's belief alone is the ground under Article 27(1)`
    `the Commissioner's belief must also be borne out under Article 27(1)`

-- F8.15: Article 27(4) says the steps "may include" the suspension, removal or replacement of "the governor referred to in that paragraph" when the notice is under (1)(c) or (d).
DECLARE `Which notices may require a governor to be suspended, removed or replaced` IS ONE OF
    `only a notice under Article 27(1)(c) or (d) may require a governor to be suspended, removed or replaced`
    `a notice on any ground in Article 27(1) may require a governor to be suspended, removed or replaced`

-- F8.16: Article 33(2)(a) "a decision of the Commissioner to deregister the charity"; Article 15(3)(a) is a deregistration the charity itself applied for.
DECLARE `Whether Article 33(2)(a) reaches a deregistration on the charity's own application` IS ONE OF
    `Article 33(2)(a) reaches a deregistration granted on the charity's own application`
    `Article 33(2)(a) does not reach a deregistration granted on the charity's own application`

-- F8.17: Article 26(2)(b) "a governor or former governor of a registered charity or of an entity that was formerly a registered charity".
DECLARE `When a person must have been a governor to fall within Article 26(2)(b)` IS ONE OF
    `a governor at any time of an entity registered at any time falls within Article 26(2)(b)`
    `a person falls within Article 26(2)(b) only if a governor while the entity was registered`

-- F8.18: Article 33(5) "on the ground that, at both the time of the application and the time of the appeal – (a) ... or (b) ...".
DECLARE `How the two grounds of Article 33(5) combine with the two times` IS ONE OF
    `each ground of Article 33(5) must hold at both times`
    `some ground of Article 33(5) must hold at each of the two times`

-- F8.19: Article 26(4)(a) "a governor or employee of the registered charity", where Article 26(2) also reaches a formerly registered entity.
DECLARE `Which charity Article 26(4)(a) speaks of` IS ONE OF
    `the registered charity of Article 26(4)(a) is a charity registered now`
    `the registered charity of Article 26(4)(a) is the charity or formerly registered entity demanded of`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The one record that carries the fork points.  Every public decision of G8 that depends on a fork takes this record as an ordinary GIVEN.
-- The field typed with the domain enumeration `Unit of a term of imprisonment` (F8.8) must be set by the integrator from the same value as the
-- corresponding fields of G6 (F6.16), G7 (F7.8) and G9 (F9.13): IP35.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `Interpretation of Articles 26 to 36`
    HAS `when the retention year of Article 26(5) starts` IS A `When the retention year of Article 26(5) starts` @desc F8.1. Taken - the year runs from the day the document is provided or retained under Article 26(4)(a); other - from the day of the notice under Article 26(1)
            TYPICALLY `the year of Article 26(5) runs from the day the document is provided or retained`
        `how promptness under Article 26(6) is judged` IS A `How promptness under Article 26(6) is judged` @desc F8.2. Taken - as soon as practicable is a judgement the caller supplies; other - a number of days from the request (the day of the request not counted), or the same with the day of the request counted as the first
            TYPICALLY `promptness under Article 26(6) is a judgement the caller supplies`
        `whether Article 28(1)(a) reaches a philosophical belief purpose` IS A `Whether Article 28(1)(a) reaches a philosophical belief purpose` @desc F8.3. Taken - only a purpose within Article 6(1)(c); other - a philosophical belief purpose counts too
            TYPICALLY `only a purpose within Article 6(1)(c) counts under Article 28(1)(a)`
        `whether the list of appealable decisions in Article 33 is closed` IS A `Whether the list of appealable decisions in Article 33 is closed` @desc F8.4. Taken - the list is closed; other - an unlisted decision of the same kind is appealable by analogy
            TYPICALLY `the list of appealable decisions in Article 33 is closed`
        `on what ground a decision of the tribunal is appealed to the court` IS A `On what ground a decision of the tribunal is appealed to the court` @desc F8.5. Taken - only the ground in Article 35(1); other - any ground in Article 34(1)
            TYPICALLY `a decision of the tribunal is appealed to the court only on the ground in Article 35(1)`
        `from when an appeal time limit under Article 36(2) runs` IS A `From when an appeal time limit under Article 36(2) runs` @desc F8.6. Taken - from the notice of the decision; other - from the decision
            TYPICALLY `an appeal time limit under Article 36(2) runs from the notice of the decision`
        `how a period fixed by a notice under Article 26 or 27 is counted` IS A `How a period fixed by a notice under Article 26 or 27 is counted` @desc F8.7. Taken - the day of service is not counted; other - the day of service is the first day
            TYPICALLY `the day of service is not counted in a period fixed by a notice`
        `unit of the terms of imprisonment in Articles 26 and 29` IS A `Unit of a term of imprisonment` @desc F8.8 (IP35). Taken - calendar months; other - days (3 months is 90 days, 2 years is 730 days)
            TYPICALLY `calendar months`
        `where the retention year of Article 26(5) ends` IS A `Where the retention year of Article 26(5) ends` @desc F8.9. Taken - on the anniversary of the day it starts; other - on the day before the anniversary
            TYPICALLY `the year of Article 26(5) ends on the anniversary of the day it starts`
        `how a year is added to 29 February under Article 26(5)` IS A `How a year is added to 29 February under Article 26(5)` @desc F8.10. Taken - a year from 29 February ends on 28 February; other - on 1 March
            TYPICALLY `a year of Article 26(5) from 29 February ends on 28 February`
        `which consents Article 29(1) requires` IS A `Which consents Article 29(1) requires` @desc F8.11. Taken - both consents are required; other - either consent suffices
            TYPICALLY `Article 29(1) requires both consents`
        `whether the first day counts in an appeal time limit under Article 36(2)` IS A `Whether the first day counts in an appeal time limit under Article 36(2)` @desc F8.12. Taken - the day of the anchor is not counted; other - it is the first day
            TYPICALLY `the day of the anchor is not counted in an appeal time limit`
        `who is excluded from appealing under Article 33(5)` IS A `Who is excluded from appealing under Article 33(5)` @desc F8.13. Taken - any applicant for registration or registered charity; other - only the applicant concerned and the charity it became
            TYPICALLY `any applicant for registration or registered charity is excluded from appealing under Article 33(5)`
        `what Article 27(1) requires of the Commissioner's belief` IS A `What Article 27(1) requires of the Commissioner's belief` @desc F8.14. Taken - the belief alone; other - the belief must also be borne out
            TYPICALLY `the Commissioner's belief alone is the ground under Article 27(1)`
        `which notices may require a governor to be suspended, removed or replaced` IS A `Which notices may require a governor to be suspended, removed or replaced` @desc F8.15. Taken - only a notice under Article 27(1)(c) or (d); other - a notice on any ground
            TYPICALLY `only a notice under Article 27(1)(c) or (d) may require a governor to be suspended, removed or replaced`
        `whether Article 33(2)(a) reaches a deregistration on the charity's own application` IS A `Whether Article 33(2)(a) reaches a deregistration on the charity's own application` @desc F8.16. Taken - it does; other - it does not
            TYPICALLY `Article 33(2)(a) reaches a deregistration granted on the charity's own application`
        `when a person must have been a governor to fall within Article 26(2)(b)` IS A `When a person must have been a governor to fall within Article 26(2)(b)` @desc F8.17. Taken - at any time of an entity registered at any time; other - while the entity was registered
            TYPICALLY `a governor at any time of an entity registered at any time falls within Article 26(2)(b)`
        `how the two grounds of Article 33(5) combine with the two times` IS A `How the two grounds of Article 33(5) combine with the two times` @desc F8.18. Taken - each ground must hold at both times; other - some ground must hold at each of the two times
            TYPICALLY `each ground of Article 33(5) must hold at both times`
        `which charity Article 26(4)(a) speaks of` IS A `Which charity Article 26(4)(a) speaks of` @desc F8.19. Taken - a charity registered now; other - the charity or formerly registered entity demanded of
            TYPICALLY `the registered charity of Article 26(4)(a) is a charity registered now`

§ `Part 7 -- Information and enforcement: the acts`

-- What is done by the persons the Law names in Articles 26 to 31.  Each constructor says what is done, not which Article does it.
DECLARE `Act under Article 26 to 31` IS ONE OF
    `serve a notice in writing requiring information, a document or attendance`
    `retain or copy a document provided and require an explanation of it`
    `require a statement of where a document that was not provided is`
    `supply a copy of a retained document`
    `comply with a requirement imposed under Article 26`
    `provide information to the Commissioner`
        HAS `known by the person to be false in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person knows the information is false in a material particular
            `intended to be used for an application or for deciding whether to serve a required steps notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person intends the Commissioner to use the information for an application for registration or for determining whether to serve a required steps notice
    `serve a required steps notice`
    `make an Order on the procedure for and restrictions on serving a required steps notice`
    `make an Order categorizing registered charities as organized religious charities`
    `grant or withdraw status as an organized religious charity`
    `disclose restricted information`
    `disclose information to the Comptroller`
    `disclose information to the Jersey Financial Services Commission`
    `prescribe by Regulations other circumstances of permitted disclosure`

§ `Part 8 -- Appeals to the Charity Tribunal: the acts`

DECLARE `Way of determining an appeal` IS ONE OF
    `remit the decision to the Commissioner`
    `remit the decision to the tribunal`
    `substitute the decision of the tribunal or court for that of the Commissioner`
    `substitute the decision of the court for that of the tribunal`
    `dismiss the appeal`

DECLARE `Act under Article 32 to 36` IS ONE OF
    `make an interim order on an appeal or reference`
    `consider evidence put to the Commissioner or accept other evidence`
    `determine an appeal in one of the ways Part 8 allows`
        HAS `way of determining the appeal` IS A `Way of determining an appeal` @desc The way the tribunal or court determines the appeal
    `award costs`
    `make a recommendation to the Commissioner`
    `refer a point of law to the court`
    `reconsider a decision of the Commissioner or of the Commissioner's staff`
    `make an Order prescribing time limits for appeals`
    `make an Order providing for notice of decisions and of reasons for them`
    `order that a substituted decision takes effect from a date`

§ `Article 26 -- the nouns`

-- The persons who can be demanded of: 26(2).  The capacity says how the person stands to the entity; the entity's own standing is separate.
DECLARE `Capacity of a person under Article 26(2)` IS ONE OF
    `the entity itself`
    `a governor or former governor of the entity`
    `a person of any other description`

DECLARE `Person addressed by a notice under Article 26` HAS
    `capacity of the person under Article 26(2)` IS A `Capacity of a person under Article 26(2)` @desc How the person stands to the entity: the entity itself, a governor or former governor of the entity, or a person of any other description
    `standing of the entity on the register` IS A `Standing on the register` @desc Where the entity (the person addressed, or the entity the governor is or was a governor of) stands on the register on the day of the notice
    `the entity was formerly a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the entity was at an earlier time a registered charity, however it stands now (an entity in the historic section is formerly registered whatever this says)
    `governor while the entity was registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only read for a governor or former governor: TRUE if the person was a governor of the entity at a time when the entity was a registered charity (TRUE for a current governor of a registered charity)

-- Why the Commissioner asks: 26(1) names one purpose; 26(10) names two (T23).
DECLARE `Purpose of a demand for information` IS ONE OF
    `determining whether to serve a required steps notice`
    `an application for registration`
    `some other purpose`

DECLARE `Demand for information under Article 26(1)` HAS
    `purpose of the demand` IS A `Purpose of a demand for information` @desc Why the Commissioner wants the information or attendance
    `the Commissioner reasonably requires what is demanded for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The Commissioner's reasonable requirement is a judgement the caller supplies (Article 26(1)(a) and (b))

DECLARE `Effect on a lien of providing a document` IS ONE OF
    `the lien is unaffected by the provision`
    `there is no lien for Article 26(3) to preserve`

-- 26(4)(a): from whom an explanation may be required.
DECLARE `Person asked for an explanation of a document` HAS
    `provided the document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the person is the person who provided the document
    `appears to be in possession of relevant information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The Commissioner's view
    `appears to be a governor or employee of the charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The Commissioner's view
    `the charity is registered now` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the entity is a registered charity (general or restricted section) on the day
    `the entity was formerly a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the entity was a registered charity earlier and is not one now

-- 26(5): what the retention period reads.
DECLARE `Facts of the retention of a document under Article 26(5)` HAS
    `day the document was provided or retained` IS A DATE @desc The day the document, copy or extract was provided to or retained or taken by the Commissioner under Article 26(4)(a)
    `day of the notice` IS A DATE @desc The day of the notice under Article 26(1) that required the document
    `day proceedings were commenced` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc NOTHING if no proceedings to which the document is relevant have been commenced against any person; otherwise the day the first were commenced
    `day proceedings concluded` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc NOTHING if those proceedings have not concluded (or none were commenced); otherwise the day they concluded

DECLARE `End of the retention of a document under Article 26(5)` IS ONE OF
    `retention is permitted up to and including`
        HAS `last day` IS A DATE @desc The last day on which the document may be retained
    `retention is permitted until proceedings conclude, and they have not concluded`

-- 26(6): the copy.
DECLARE `Request for a copy of a retained document` HAS
    `the person requires the document for the purpose of the person's business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Article 26(6): the person needs the document for business
    `the person has requested the document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person has asked for the document
    `day of the request` IS A DATE @desc The day the person requested the document
    `day the copy was supplied` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc NOTHING if no copy has been supplied yet

-- 26(7): a contravention of a requirement.
DECLARE `Facts of a contravention under Article 26(7)` HAS
    `the requirement was validly imposed under Article 26(1) or (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Established by Art 26(1) and Art 26(4) rules: a notice in writing was served on a person within Article 26(2) for a permitted purpose, or the Article 26(4) conditions are met
    `the person did what was required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person complied with the requirement (in the time specified)
    `what is withheld is subject to legal professional privilege` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Article 26(8): the person would in an action in court be entitled to refuse to disclose or produce it on grounds of legal professional privilege
    `the person has a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person has a reasonable excuse for the contravention - a judgement the caller supplies

-- 26(9): the statement.
DECLARE `Proceedings in which a statement is tendered` IS ONE OF
    `criminal proceedings for an offence under Article 26(7)`
    `criminal proceedings for an offence under Article 26(10)`
    `any other criminal proceedings`
    `proceedings that are not criminal proceedings`

DECLARE `Statement made under Article 26` HAS
    `made in compliance with a requirement imposed under Article 26` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the statement was made in compliance with a requirement imposed under Article 26
    `tendered against the person who made it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the prosecution would use it in evidence against the person who made it
    `proceedings` IS A `Proceedings in which a statement is tendered` @desc The proceedings in which the prosecution would use it

-- 26(10) and (11): false information.
DECLARE `Facts of providing information under Article 26(10)` HAS
    `the person provided information to the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person provided information to the Commissioner
    `known by the person to be false in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person knew the information was false in a material particular
    `intended for an application for registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person intended the Commissioner to use it for the purpose of an application for registration
    `intended for deciding whether to serve a required steps notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person intended the Commissioner to use it for the purpose of determining whether to serve a required steps notice
    `contained in a document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Article 26(11)(a): irrelevant to the offence
    `provided under Article 26` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Article 26(11)(b): irrelevant to the offence

-- The time a notice specifies: 26(1)(a), (b) and 27(2).
DECLARE `Time specified in a notice` IS ONE OF
    `a date fixed by the notice`
        HAS date IS A DATE @desc The day by which the notice requires the thing to be done
    `a period of days fixed by the notice`
        HAS days IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days after the day of service within which the notice requires the thing to be done

-- The offences of Articles 26 and 29, for the penalties.
DECLARE `Offence under Article 26 or 29` IS ONE OF
    `the offence of contravening a requirement under Article 26(1) or (4)`
    `the offence of providing false information under Article 26(10)`
    `the offence of disclosing restricted information under Article 29(1)`

§ `Articles 27 and 28 -- the nouns`

DECLARE `Kind of requirement in a required steps notice` IS ONE OF
    `a requirement to suspend a governor`
    `a requirement to remove a governor`
    `a requirement to replace a governor`
    `any other requirement`

DECLARE `Requirement in a required steps notice` HAS
    `kind of requirement` IS A `Kind of requirement in a required steps notice` @desc What the requirement requires: to suspend, remove or replace a governor, or anything else
    `the governor concerned is a governor of the charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only read for a requirement about a governor: TRUE if the governor is a governor of the charity on which the notice was served, or of the charity of which the person served is a governor

-- How an Order under Article 28 treats one charity (28(1), 28(2)(a)); the content of the Order is an input.
DECLARE `Order under Article 28 as it applies to a charity` HAS
    `the Order categorizes the charity as an organized religious charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Article 28(1): whether the Order categorizes this charity
    `the Order gives the Commissioner discretion to grant or withdraw the status` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Article 28(2)(a)
    `the Commissioner has granted the status` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only read if the Order gives the Commissioner discretion
    `the Commissioner has withdrawn the status` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only read if the Order gives the Commissioner discretion

§ `Articles 29 to 31 -- the nouns`

DECLARE `Information received and its character` HAS
    `relates to the business or other affairs of a person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Article 29(1): the information relates to the business or other affairs of any person
    `received under or for the purposes of this Law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Article 29(1)(a)
    `received directly or indirectly from a person who so received it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Article 29(1)(b)
    `already made available to the public from other sources` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Article 29(2)(b): at the time of the disclosure it is or has already been made available to the public from other sources
    `in the form of a summary or collection that identifies no particular person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Article 29(2)(c): so framed as not to enable information relating to any particular person to be ascertained from it

DECLARE `Recipient of a disclosure of information` IS ONE OF
    `a disclosure to the Comptroller`
    `a disclosure to the Jersey Financial Services Commission`
    `a disclosure to the Attorney General, the Bailiff or the court`
    `a disclosure to any other person`

DECLARE `Disclosure of information` HAS
    `by or on behalf of the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the disclosure is made by or on behalf of the Commissioner
    `recipient` IS A `Recipient of a disclosure of information` @desc To whom the information is disclosed
    `to enable the Commissioner to discharge a function` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Article 31(a): the purpose is to enable the Commissioner to discharge any of the Commissioner's functions
    `to enable the recipient to discharge a function` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Articles 31(b) and (c): the purpose is to enable the Comptroller or the JFSC to discharge any of its functions
    `to enable the recipient to discharge a function in relation to charities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Article 31(d): the purpose is to enable the Attorney General, the Bailiff or the court to discharge any of their functions in relation to charities, under this Law, a constitutional Law, the customary law or any other law
    `for the investigation or prosecution of an offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Article 31(e): for the investigation or prosecution of any offence under any enactment or under the customary law of Jersey
    `for taking or deciding whether to take proceedings under this Law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Article 31(e)
    `in circumstances prescribed by Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Article 31(f): the circumstances are prescribed by the States by Regulations (the content of the Regulations is an input)
    `required by the recipient for its functions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Article 30: the Comptroller, for its taxation functions in relation to registered charities or other entities with charitable purposes, or the JFSC, for its functions under the Non-Profit Organizations (Jersey) Law 2008, requires the information
    `consent of the person to whom the information relates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Article 29(1)
    `consent of the person from whom the information was received` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Article 29(1): read only where Article 29(1)(b) applies

DECLARE `Provision of Article 31 that permits a disclosure` IS ONE OF
    `Article 31(a)`
    `Article 31(b)`
    `Article 31(c)`
    `Article 31(d)`
    `Article 31(e)`
    `Article 31(f)`

§ `Articles 32 to 36 -- the nouns`

-- Who is appealing and what they stand as.  The flags are independent facts, not exclusive kinds: a registered charity may also be the person served with a notice.
DECLARE `Appellant under Article 33` HAS
    `an applicant for registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the appellant is an applicant for registration
    `a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the appellant is a registered charity (general or restricted section)
    `the Attorney General` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the appellant is the Attorney General
    `a person served with the notice that contains the requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Article 33(3): whether the appellant is the person on whom the Commissioner served the notice under Article 26 or the required steps notice
    `a person with an interest in the registered name of the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Article 33(5)(b)

-- What Article 33 is asked about: who appeals, and which decision.  The decision is the domain record (subject and outcome): IP27.
DECLARE `Appeal under Article 33` HAS
    appellant IS AN `Appellant under Article 33` @desc Who is appealing
    `decision appealed` IS A `Decision of the Commissioner` @desc The decision of the Commissioner appealed against: which decision, and whether the Commissioner did what was sought or proposed or refused
    `the decision concerns the appellant's own application or registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the applicant refused, or the charity deregistered or refused permission or approval, is the appellant itself (Article 33(1) and (2) speak of the applicant and the charity)

-- Which paragraph of Article 33 gives the right, if any.  The last constructor is the answer "no appeal is given by Part 8", which is not a statement that no other remedy exists (Article 40(1) preserves independent powers).
DECLARE `Right of appeal under Article 33` IS ONE OF
    `a right of appeal under Article 33(1)(a)`
    `a right of appeal under Article 33(1)(b)`
    `a right of appeal under Article 33(2)(a)`
    `a right of appeal under Article 33(2)(b)`
    `a right of appeal under Article 33(2)(c)`
    `a right of appeal under Article 33(2)(d)`
    `a right of appeal under Article 33(2)(e)`
    `a right of appeal under Article 33(3)`
    `a right of appeal under Article 33(4)`
    `a right of appeal under Article 33(5)(a)`
    `a right of appeal under Article 33(5)(b)`
    `a right of appeal under Article 33(5) on grounds that differ between the two times`
    `a right of appeal by analogy with Article 33(1)(b)`
    `a right of appeal by analogy with Article 33(2)(a)`
    `no appeal is given by Part 8`

-- Article 34(1) and Article 35(1): the complaint made against the decision.
DECLARE `Standard that a decision is said to fall short of` IS ONE OF
    `wrong`
    `unreasonable`
    `neither wrong nor unreasonable`

DECLARE `Respect in which a decision is said to fall short` IS ONE OF
    `its merits`
    `the facts`
    `the law`
    `all the circumstances of the case`
    `some other respect`

DECLARE `Ground alleged in an appeal` HAS
    `standard alleged` IS A `Standard that a decision is said to fall short of` @desc Whether the decision is said to be wrong, or unreasonable, or neither
    `respect alleged` IS A `Respect in which a decision is said to fall short` @desc In which respect: its merits, the facts, the law, all the circumstances of the case, or some other

-- Article 36(2)(a): what an Order may prescribe.  The Order is not in the sources, so a caller supplies it or the rule refuses.
DECLARE `Time limit prescribed under Article 36(2)(a)` IS ONE OF
    `no Order has prescribed a time limit`
    `an Order prescribes a time limit of days`
        HAS days IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days within which the appeal must be brought, counted from the day the reading chosen for Article 36(2) fixes

DECLARE `Dates of an appeal under Article 36(2)` HAS
    `day of the decision` IS A DATE @desc The day of the decision of the Commissioner (or of the tribunal, for an appeal to the court)
    `day of the notice of the decision` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc NOTHING if notice of the decision has not been given; otherwise the day it was given
    `day the appeal was lodged` IS A DATE @desc The day the appeal was brought
